---
config:
  theme: dark
  look: handDrawn
---
sequenceDiagram
 participant browser
 participant server

 %% the browser first sends a GET request to the server and fetches the document (notes)
 browser->>server: GET https://studies.cs.helsinki.fi/exampleapp/notes 
 activate server
 %% then the server sends the HTML file to the browser and 200 OK means that it was successful
 server->>browser: 200 OK (Content-Type: text/html)
 deactivate server

 %% the HTML file contains two things: 1. <link> for css stylesheet and  <script> for Javascript file
 %% so the html file makes the browser send two more Get request for the .css and .js files from the server
 browser->>server: GET https://studies.cs.helsinki.fi/exampleapp/main.css
 activate server
 server->>browser: 200 OK (Content-Type: text/css)
 deactivate server
 %% And for the js file:
 browser->>server: GET https://studies.cs.helsinki.fi/exampleapp/main.js
 activate server
 server->>browser: 200 OK (Content-Type: application/javascript)
 deactivate server

 %% When browser executes the js file, it reaches here: xhttp.open("GET", "/exampleapp/data.json", true)
 %% so the browser will send another GET request to the server for fetching the JSON file
 note right of browser: the browser starts executing the javascript and fetching the JSON File
 browser->>server: GET https://studies.cs.helsinki.fi/exampleapp/data.json
 activate server
 server->>browser: 200 OK (Content-Type: application/json) <-> [{content: "fggfg", date: "..."},…]
 deactivate server
 %% xhttp.onreadystatechange callback handles rendering the notes
 %% the javascript will get the data and for example, it will add it to a list

 note right of browser: the callback function is executed by the browser so the notes gets rendered
 note right of browser: + User writes a note (for example: test) and clicks on "Save" (/new_note)
 %% When the user clicks on the submit ("save") button, browser will execute the /new_note form with POST action
 browser->>server: POST https://studies.cs.helsinki.fi/exampleapp/new_note (Form Data: note=test)
 activate server
 %% Server returns status code 302 Found that is a URL Redirect so it asks the browser to send a GET request for location "notes"
 note left of server: new notes will be pushed to an array in the server so they will be visible until the server restarts
 server->>browser: 302 Found (URL redirect) Location: notes
 deactivate server
 note left of server: the server asks the browser for a new GET request to "notes" (which is a reload)
  browser->>server: GET https://studies.cs.helsinki.fi/exampleapp/notes 
 activate server
 %% then the server sends the HTML file to the browser and 200 OK means that it was successful
 server->>browser: 200 OK (Content-Type: text/html)
 deactivate server
 %% the HTML file contains two things: 1. <link> for css stylesheet and  <script> for Javascript file
 %% so the html file makes the browser send two more Get request for the .css and .js files from the server
 browser->>server: GET https://studies.cs.helsinki.fi/exampleapp/main.css
 activate server
 server->>browser: 200 OK (Content-Type: text/css)
 deactivate server
 %% And for the js file:
 browser->>server: GET https://studies.cs.helsinki.fi/exampleapp/main.js
 activate server
 server->>browser: 200 OK (Content-Type: application/javascript)
 deactivate server
 %% the "test" note can be viewed in the Network Tab -> new_note -> Payload -> form data
 
 %% When browser executes the js file, it reaches here: xhttp.open("GET", "/exampleapp/data.json", true)
 %% so the browser will send another GET request to the server for fetching the JSON file
 note right of browser: the browser starts executing the javascript and fetching the JSON File
 browser->>server: GET https://studies.cs.helsinki.fi/exampleapp/data.json
 activate server
 server->>browser: 200 OK (Content-Type: application/json) <-> [{content: "test", date: "..."},…]
 deactivate server
 %% xhttp.onreadystatechange callback handles rendering the notes:
 note right of browser: the javascript will get the data, and for example, it will add it to a list so the user can view it